    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="6fbea3e5-7027-50db-b370-95a1e7560208" activityNameId="409efa6a-f14b-5601-8e2a-6c2015f895c8" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Basic oxygen furnace gas, burned in power plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Basic oxygen furnace gas, burned in power plant
na;
UUID: 7b5b44c9-1e9b-368e-bfaa-20c395e80c8d
The module does not include input of fuel (basic oxygen furnace gas) because BOF gas is treated as a waste product of steel production (i.e. zero allocation to blast furnace gas). Nevertheless, the module includes the emissions caused by the burning of the gas in the power plant. It includes also power plant infrastructure.The inventory includes specific emissions to air from a basic oxygen furnace with supressed combustion after abatement. 
Location: Data from literature, referring to Europe
Technology: Industry data.
Time period: Time of publications.
Production volume: na
Sampling: Data from literature 
Extrapolations: Some generic datasets from ecoinvent have been used.
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_7b5b44c9-1e9b-368e-bfaa-20c395e80c8d.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
